                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "92ee6a3b-e69a-4418-bad3-56537804f591",
                        "source_entry_id": "c55608b3-e67c-3c4e-9e90-d1413433e6f3",
                        "source_sense_id": "76bbe87a-24e4-3f47-a801-286ff5804fb5",
                        "target_lang_word": "confabulation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "confabulation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46822fcb-c87e-3705-a8f8-ac3cc98d2c90",
                                        "entry_id": "778dd471-9db0-3290-9881-a2f89c0a6a31",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A casual conversation; a chat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "663bfd51-f625-417c-bb77-0ca238028fd7",
                                                "sense_id": "46822fcb-c87e-3705-a8f8-ac3cc98d2c90",
                                                "text": "[…] Mrs Grantly was preparing herself for a grand attack which she was to make on her father, as agreed upon between herself and her husband during their curtain confabulation of that morning."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd7b9e4b-1248-4d8c-bdf1-437176a3e9cf",
                                                "sense_id": "46822fcb-c87e-3705-a8f8-ac3cc98d2c90",
                                                "text": "The schoolroom piano broke into all gruesome fancies; and when that failed there were confabulations in corners, with a sequel of one of them going out in the highest spirits in order to “come in” as something new."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30dc630a-2a65-4519-932a-aa5f3724b5d5",
                                                "sense_id": "46822fcb-c87e-3705-a8f8-ac3cc98d2c90",
                                                "text": "The vision had roused a host of other associations, and he sat looking with new eyes at the library which, for over thirty years, had been the scene of his solitary musings and of all the family confabulations."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a7c2124-83b0-377b-b132-e356dce91d75",
                                        "entry_id": "778dd471-9db0-3290-9881-a2f89c0a6a31",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fabricated memory believed to be true, especially in someone suffering from dementia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e0afe89-42d3-4d13-95f1-7c9b054bddab",
                                                "sense_id": "8a7c2124-83b0-377b-b132-e356dce91d75",
                                                "text": "For Örulv and Hydén, confabulation is ‘world-making’ (669). What the person with AD chooses to enunciate, ‘may capture something important in the way the person makes sense of his or her life and also make meaning-based connections’ (Hydén and Örulv 2009: 206)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ceb80b0-647c-447d-9aa8-44f722cda6b0",
                                                "sense_id": "8a7c2124-83b0-377b-b132-e356dce91d75",
                                                "text": "Segal said another characteristic of Trump’s questionable mental acuity is confabulation. “It’s where he takes an idea or something that’s happened and he adds to it things that have not happened.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3d396146-f082-4d7f-9ee7-f268613d7374",
                        "source_entry_id": "c55608b3-e67c-3c4e-9e90-d1413433e6f3",
                        "source_sense_id": "76bbe87a-24e4-3f47-a801-286ff5804fb5",
                        "target_lang_word": "confabulation",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "confabulation",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09c9b470-f65f-3f71-9dff-4d8ff892bde6",
                                        "entry_id": "7d18a2de-e7f1-3f92-b856-bf56bd0ea7fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Action de confabuler."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ironic",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90dafeca-5ce8-4eda-b760-6dd46fe09c53",
                                                "sense_id": "09c9b470-f65f-3f71-9dff-4d8ff892bde6",
                                                "text": "« Quand j’écris et parle de moi au singulier, cela suppose une confabulation avec le lecteur ; il peut examiner, discuter, douter et même rire. Mais quand je m’arme du redoutable nous, je professe ; il faut se soumettre. »"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcf1160b-e3ec-4e6c-9660-7707603fc689",
                                                "sense_id": "09c9b470-f65f-3f71-9dff-4d8ff892bde6",
                                                "text": "Ils veulent bien tout peser et tout contrôler, hormis ce qui dépasse l’apparence et la confabulation humaine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcfa8b05-e2db-425a-8eac-31695c4463a4",
                                                "sense_id": "09c9b470-f65f-3f71-9dff-4d8ff892bde6",
                                                "text": "Voilà ce qui m’arrive régulièrement quand je suis acculé à la confabulation, je crois sincèrement avoir répondu aux questions qu’on me pose et en réalité il n’en est rien."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3aca39c5-95f9-4a76-b779-1e9122544c9f",
                                                "sense_id": "09c9b470-f65f-3f71-9dff-4d8ff892bde6",
                                                "text": "Ils étaient en confabulation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1a66b4b-b90d-34e0-b7e2-2ca542ccce97",
                                        "entry_id": "7d18a2de-e7f1-3f92-b856-bf56bd0ea7fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Production imaginaire, prise pour un souvenir, venant combler une lacune de mémoire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28e76551-c3dd-4687-a1f2-050a241abdf5",
                                                "sense_id": "c1a66b4b-b90d-34e0-b7e2-2ca542ccce97",
                                                "text": "Examinant une expérience relatée par Oliver Sacks, elle affirme qu '« Un cas très sévère d'amnésie avec confabulation ( ... ) peut conduire à conclure , comme le fait l'auteur , que le patient privé du récit de la continuité de sa vie, a perdu avec son histoire le soubassement de sa personne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
